# An allowlist, not a blocklist: the image runs `python -m mcp_wiki` from
# /code with its dependencies installed into /venv from pyproject.toml and
# uv.lock, so those, the package and the license files are all it needs.
# Everything else — docs and their GIFs/diagrams, tests, scripts, release
# metadata, and local leftovers such as .venv, coverage, dist/, .archify/ or
# Claude worktrees — stays out of both the build context and the image,
# including whatever new clutter appears in the checkout later.
*
!mcp_wiki
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!LICENSE
!NOTICE

# Bytecode from a local run must not shadow the sources.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
